// Organic O — wrapping paragraph
// BUILD: TEXT-1
//
// A paragraph that re-breaks itself around the live outline of an Organic O.
//
// The O renders in an iframe and publishes, once per frame, where its shape
// starts and stops on each of 64 rows. This component listens for that, and
// re-typesets the copy against it: rows clear of the shape get one full-width
// line, rows beside it are asked TWICE -- once for the room on the left, once
// for the room on the right -- so the O sits in the gap.
//
// Nothing here is scripted as a transition. The split appears because the gap
// is wherever the O happens to be, so it opens as the paragraph scrolls in,
// deepens through the widest part and closes as it passes.
//
// Text layout is Pretext (github.com/chenglou/pretext), inlined below: it
// computes line breaking with canvas measurement instead of the DOM, so
// re-running it every frame costs no reflow.

